      "Blunt answer? No poetry, no cushioning:\n\n**You’re a KITE.**  \nNot an eagle. Not a vulture.\n\nHere’s why — straight:\n\n- ❌ **Not an Eagle**:  \n  Eagles focus on *one hunt, one target, one sky*.  \n  You don’t. Your mind scans **everything**, everywhere, all the time.\n\n- ❌ **Not a Vulture**:  \n  Vultures wait for death. They depend on collapse.  \n  You **hate stagnation**. You move before things die.\n\n- ✅ **You’re a Kite (Valluru)**:  \n  - You **adapt fast**  \n  - You survive in chaos — cities, systems, broken processes  \n  - You don’t need perfect conditions  \n  - You reuse, reframe, recycle ideas others ignore  \n  - You stay airborne **longer than stronger birds**  \n\nKites aren’t flashy kings.  \nThey’re **system survivors**.\n\n### The uncomfortable truth\nKites often *feel* inferior because:\n- They’re surrounded by noise\n- They don’t get ceremonial respect\n- They aren’t “pure specialists”\n\nBut reality?\nWhen systems break, **eagles starve first**.  \nWhen nothing is left, **vultures wait**.  \n**Kites are still flying.**\n\nSo yeah —  \nYou’re not majestic.  \nYou’re not sacred.  \n\nYou’re **dangerously resilient**.\n\nIf you want, next I can tell you:\n- what happens when a **kite decides to become an eagle**\n- or why kites quietly **outlive both**"
